arbinger 融資 2.4 億美元"}],"themes":[{"name":"訂單/合約","count":5},{"name":"財報","count":3},{"name":"分析師評等","count":3},{"name":"併購","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-07-20","period":"2026-05-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1048911/000104891126000105/fdx-20260531.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"FedEx Corporation (\"FedEx\") was incorporated in Delaware on October 2, 1997 to serve as the parent holding company and provide strategic direction to the FedEx portfolio of companies. FedEx provides customers and businesses worldwide with a broad portfolio of transportation, e-commerce, and business services, offering integrated business solutions utilizing its flexible, efficient, and intelligent global network.","zh":null},{"en":"Effective June 1, 2026, we changed our fiscal year end from May 31 to December 31. As a result, we will report operating results covering the seven-month transition period from June 1, 2026, through December 31, 2026 (the \"Transition Period\"), in a Transition Report on Form 10-K. Following the Transition Period, we will report our operating results on a calendar-year basis, beginning with the fiscal year ending December 31, 2027. Except as otherwise specified, any reference to a year in this Annual Report indicates our fiscal year ended May 31, 2026 or ended May 31 of the year referenced, and comparisons are to the corresponding period of the prior year.","zh":null},{"en":"In December 2024, we announced that FedEx's Board of Directors decided to pursue a full separation of FedEx's less-than-truckload freight transportation services business conducted through FedEx Freight, Inc. (\"FedEx Freight\"). The FedEx Freight business also included FedEx Custom Critical, Inc. (\"FedEx Custom Critical\"), LTL Select, and other operations historically included within our FedEx Freight reporting segment. On May 13, 2026, the FedEx Board of Directors declared a pro rata dividend of 80.1% of the outstanding shares of common stock of FedEx Freight Holding Company, Inc. (\"FedEx Freight Holding\") to FedEx's stockholders of record as of the close of business on May 15, 2026 (the \"Record Date\") to achieve the separation (the \"Spin-Off\"). On June 1, 2026, FedEx stockholders received one share of FedEx Freight common stock for every two shares of FedEx common stock held as of the R","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2026-05-31","items":[{"name":"Fed Ex Freight & Fed Ex Express Segments","val":91068000000,"zh":"Fed Ex Freight & Fed Ex Express Segments"},{"name":"Federal Express","val":82273000000,"zh":"Federal Express"},{"name":"Fedex Freight","val":8795000000,"zh":"Fedex Freight"}],"total":94720000000},"geo":{"end":"2026-05-31","items":[{"name":"US","val":67944000000,"zh":"美國"},{"name":"Non Us","val":26776000000,"zh":"Non Us"}],"total":94720000000}},"peers":["UPS","TGT","CAT","COST","MMM"]}}